From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:51:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: TerminalApp: an agent bridge for the system's agent
 host

AgentBridgeProvider lets a caller holding ACCESS_AGENT_BRIDGE
(signature|privileged), on OpenBook Quire core, reach the guest's
quired on vsock port 7690 while the Linux environment runs. Only the
VM's owner may have a vsock to it, so the provider asks virtmgr for the
connection (VirtualMachine.connectVsock) and relays it to one end of a
socket pair. Other guest ports (ttyd, the guest agent) are not offered.

Also: Cuttlefish products not named vsoc_* get the emulator boot
timeout, found by ro.boot.hypervisor.version (cf-crosvm, cf-qemu); the
Debian guest runs under nested KVM there.

OpenBook ANAL-218 (Quire Q4).
